      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The correlation you observe is likely due to the \"confirmation bias,\" where you selectively notice successes that align with your synchronization belief while overlooking unrelated outcomes. In psychology, this state is often called the \"self-fulfilling prophecy,\" where focusing intensely on a goal changes your behavior, communication, or decision-making, thereby increasing the likelihood of success regardless of any supernatural influence. While there is no scientific evidence that your thoughts directly manipulate physical laws or external timing, your heightened focus almost certainly provides the mental discipline needed to realize your objectives. Consequently, the \"mechanism\" at work is your own powerful agency and preparation, which makes the events feel extra meaningful and precisely timed.",
